senses.gloss:
आ॑सक्त a. suspended, hanging on;
 clinging, attached, or
used to;
 intent on (loc. or —˚).

आसक्ति॑ f. adhering, clinging to, pursuit, devotion;
 as
adv. coherently, entirely.

अशङ्क a. without fear or doubt;
 n. adv.;
 f. अशङ्का no
fear or hesitation.

आशङ्का f. fear, apprehension of (abl.);
 distrust. —
˚शल्य n. the dart or thorn of fear.*

अश˚ङ्कित a. without fear or doubt;
 n. adv.;
 f. अशङ्का
no fear or hesitation.

आ॑सन n. sitting, sitting down;
 the way of sitting ((r.));
sitting quiet, halting;
 seat, throne, high position.

आसन॑ n. sitting, sitting down;
 the way of sitting ((r.));
sitting quiet, halting;
 seat, throne, high position.

आ॑सन्न a. set, put down, reached, got;
 come to, neared,
approached;
 proximate, near, next, imminent. n. proximity.

अशरण a. unprotected;
 n. want of protection,
helplessness.

अ॑संवृत^1 a. uncovered, bare;
 n. a cert. hell.
[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20160412. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/275. note: cf. mw 'uncovered'.

असंस्कार a. unadorned;
 m. want of ornament,
artlessness.

असंस्तुत a. not harmonizing, refractory;
 distant,
foreign.

असंक्षिप्त a. not laid down*;
 not concise, extensive,
full.

असंगीतकम् adv. without music;
 ˚नृत् dance w. m.,
i.e. do something absurd or ridiculous.*

असत्त्ववचन a. not signifying anything substantial
or material;
 abstr. ˚ता f.

असदृश a. unlike, dissimilar, incomparable;
 of unequal
birth;
 unfit, improper.

असद्ग्रह a. bent upon something evil, following a bad
caprice;
 m. bad inclination, caprice, whim.

असंभ्रम a. free from agitation, tranquil, calm;
 n.
adv.

असहन a. unable to bear (—˚);
 impatient, jealous,
envious. n. intolerance, impatience.

असहिष्णु a. unable to bear (acc., loc., or —˚);
intolerant, jealous;
 abstr. ˚ता f., ˚त्व n.

असाधन n. no means, no requisite;
 a. without means,
impossible.

असाधु॑ a. not good, bad, wicked;
 m. a bad man, a villain;
n. evil, malice, also adv.

असाध्य a. not to be overcome, impracticable, incurable,
irremediable;
 not susceptible of proof. Abstr. ˚ता f., ˚त्व n.

आशय॑ m. resting-place, couch, abode, retreat, seat, esp.
of feelings and thoughts, i.e. heart, mind;
 intention, disposition.

आशावासस् n. the sky as garment;
 acc. w. वस् put on the
garment of the sky, i.e. go naked.

2 आसाद्य ger. having reached or got;
 often = a prep. on, in,
at, with;
 according to, in consequence of (acc.).
